# Live project metrics (the "Project reach" section on the homepage)
#
# GitHub stars and forks are fetched without auth. To also show 14-day repo
# traffic (views + unique visitors), add a token with push access to the repos:
#
#   1. Create a classic Personal Access Token with the `repo` scope:
#      https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   2. Locally: copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the token below.
#   3. On Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables → add GITHUB_TOKEN.
#
# Without it the section still renders (stars/forks live); traffic shows a hint.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Owner-only dashboard (/dashboard) — the private view with every project
# (including private repos), full metrics and referrers. Set a password to
# unlock it; without one the dashboard stays locked and nothing private is shown.
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

